# Everything in the build context is uploaded to the Docker daemon and can land
# in the build cache, whether or not any COPY references it. On a deployed host
# this directory holds real secrets, so the default is deny-all and the build
# opts back in.
#
#   .env         dashboard password, CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
#   9router.env  JWT_SECRET, API_KEY_SECRET, INITIAL_PASSWORD, MACHINE_ID_SALT
#
# Both are git-ignored, which says nothing about the build context.

*

# The only path the Dockerfile copies. Re-included at the top level on purpose:
# `*` excludes the `docker` directory itself, and re-including a nested path
# under an excluded parent is the classic way to end up with an empty COPY.
!docker
